  "question": {
    "text": "In the nucleophilic substitution reactions <math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mtext>N</mtext> </msub> <mtext>2</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mrow> <mtext>or&nbsp;S</mtext></mrow> <mtext>N</mtext> </msub> <mtext>1</mtext></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math> the reactivity of alkyl halides follows the sequence"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "R-I &gt; R-Br &gt; R-Cl &gt; R-F",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "R-Cl &gt; R-F &gt; R-Br &gt; R-I",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "R-F &gt; R-Cl &gt; R-Br &gt; R-I",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "R-I &gt; R-F &gt; R-Cl &gt; R-Br",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Nucleophilic substitution reaction depends on learning group ability<br />The correct order of reactivity is<br /><math> <mrow>  <mtext>RI</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>RBr</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>RCl</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>RF&#x00A0;</mtext></mrow></math><br />It is due to fact, that weaker the base, better will be the leaving group.<br />Leaving group ability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>I</mtext> <mo>−</mo> </msup> <mo>&gt;</mo><msup> <mrow> <mtext>Br</mtext></mrow> <mo>−</mo> </msup> <mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>Cl</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msup> <mtext>F</mtext> <mo>−</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math><br />"
  }
